/**
 * hybrid-engine.ts — L1 engine core (device code: Scratch block emission).
 *
 * Faithful TS port of the block-emitting half of
 * build_ue5_lumen_hybrid.py: the 15 warp custom procedures of the UE5
 * hybrid (setup_camera, fill_tri, fill_quad_scan, draw_quad_3d,
 * render_sky, render_arch, render_smooth_cylinder, render_crystal,
 * render_floor, render_mirror_sphere, trace_refl_fast, render_rt_hero,
 * render_god_rays, sort_5_objects, render_frame) plus the flag-clicked
 * input/main loop (WASD/QE + arrows, drag + flick inertia, dirty-driven
 * rendering). Register variables and SoA scene lists follow the original
 * exactly; scene data arrives as the bake result (TempleBake) — the
 * engine reads SoA lists and registers only (design section 1).
 *
 * Ported mechanically from the Python source and verified by comparing
 * the generated sb3 against the original ue5_lumen_hybrid.sb3
 * (see tools/compare-temple.mjs). No numeric values were changed.
 */
